WEBVTT

00:04.379 --> 00:05.422
It seems there was

00:05.505 --> 00:07.632
a student general meeting the other day.

00:08.258 --> 00:09.384
I heard

00:09.467 --> 00:13.722
Masachika and the heiress of
Taniyama Heavy Industries were involved.

00:13.805 --> 00:14.889
Yes.

00:14.973 --> 00:16.099
She was your rival

00:16.182 --> 00:18.893
until the very last moment
in junior high after all.

00:18.977 --> 00:21.104
I thought she was more capable.

00:21.855 --> 00:25.483
But it seems she left
in the middle of the meeting.

00:25.567 --> 00:27.777
I'm sure she has her reasons.

00:30.071 --> 00:31.197
In any case,

00:31.281 --> 00:35.368
Masachika's reputation has been boosted.

00:35.869 --> 00:37.203
Listen up.

00:37.287 --> 00:38.788
No matter who your opponent is,

00:38.872 --> 00:40.707
you must not lose.

00:40.790 --> 00:43.251
Grandfather, I understand.

00:44.627 --> 00:47.630
You may not be as talented as Masachika,

00:48.381 --> 00:49.382
but

00:49.466 --> 00:52.886
you know the responsibility
that comes with competency.

00:52.969 --> 00:54.012
In that regard,

00:54.095 --> 00:55.305
he's beyond help.

00:56.139 --> 00:58.099
He has the greatest talent of anyone

00:58.183 --> 01:00.185
and a uniquely privileged environment,

01:00.268 --> 01:01.895
but he gave up his responsibility.

01:02.896 --> 01:05.398
That's why you must never

01:05.482 --> 01:07.400
lose to someone like him.

01:08.151 --> 01:10.487
Do you understand, Yuki?

01:10.570 --> 01:12.655
Yes, Grandfather.

01:15.533 --> 01:16.826
Yuki?

01:17.911 --> 01:18.995
Mother,

01:19.079 --> 01:20.705
is something wrong?

01:21.414 --> 01:23.208
Are you and Masachika

01:23.291 --> 01:25.335
getting along well?

01:25.418 --> 01:26.961
Yes, of course.

01:28.129 --> 01:29.297
I see.

01:29.380 --> 01:30.465
Well,

01:30.548 --> 01:32.801
is something wrong with my brother?

01:32.884 --> 01:34.135
No, it's nothing.

01:35.011 --> 01:37.889
You have a Chinese class later, right?

01:37.972 --> 01:39.557
Yes, it's a remote lesson today.

01:42.477 --> 01:43.561
Do your best.

01:44.062 --> 01:45.313
Yes.

01:49.734 --> 01:50.568
Ayano.

01:50.652 --> 01:51.986
Yes, Mistress Yuki?

01:52.070 --> 01:53.613
Let me hold you.

01:53.696 --> 01:55.615
Yes, as you wish.

02:04.290 --> 02:06.709
Good, I'm all better now.

02:06.793 --> 02:08.628
Is that all?

02:08.711 --> 02:10.296
Thank you.

02:10.380 --> 02:11.631
Oh, dear.

02:11.714 --> 02:14.008
Boobs really are great, aren't they?

03:46.976 --> 03:47.936
Yo, Kuze.

03:48.019 --> 03:50.438
Last week's general meeting was amazing.

03:50.521 --> 03:55.902
When I first heard Taniyama's argument,
I thought it was over.

03:55.985 --> 03:58.321
Which part of it was your strategy?

03:58.404 --> 04:01.908
Anyway, let me put down my stuff first.

04:04.035 --> 04:05.828
Good morning, Alya.

04:05.912 --> 04:07.330
Good morning.

04:07.413 --> 04:10.708
<i>Well, her reaction is the same as usual.</i>

04:11.834 --> 04:13.086
Alya.

04:13.169 --> 04:16.297
These guys want to hear
about your heroics last week.

04:16.381 --> 04:17.298
What?

04:17.382 --> 04:20.093
Well then, just ask Alya for the details.

04:20.176 --> 04:22.720
The gacha event is waiting for me.

04:29.644 --> 04:30.603
Kujou.

04:30.687 --> 04:32.480
Did you come up with the speech

04:32.563 --> 04:34.232
at the general meeting last week?

04:34.315 --> 04:35.149
What?

04:35.233 --> 04:38.903
Well, you could say that.

04:38.987 --> 04:40.947
It took me by surprise.

04:41.030 --> 04:43.700
I didn't know you were
so good at giving speeches.

04:43.783 --> 04:45.785
Thank you.

04:47.161 --> 04:48.871
You didn't ask any questions.

04:48.955 --> 04:50.206
Was that your strategy?

04:50.290 --> 04:51.291
Yes.

04:51.374 --> 04:54.210
That's what we decided in advance.

04:54.294 --> 04:56.879
Then, why did Kuze barge in midway?

04:56.963 --> 04:59.632
I didn't expect that either.

05:00.133 --> 05:01.217
By the way,

05:01.301 --> 05:03.886
Taniyama ran away midway.

05:03.970 --> 05:06.180
How dare she run away
from the challenge she started?

05:06.264 --> 05:07.890
That's so lame.

05:08.766 --> 05:11.102
Kuze, a minute, please.

05:13.938 --> 05:15.773
Come to think of it,

05:15.857 --> 05:17.817
the student council needs extra hands.

05:17.900 --> 05:19.986
<i>Sorry, I'll talk to you later.</i>

05:21.487 --> 05:23.614
So what's the matter?

05:24.657 --> 05:26.784
You don't want to hear Taniyama

05:26.868 --> 05:28.286
being criticized so harshly?

05:28.369 --> 05:30.079
Because Taniyama...

05:30.163 --> 05:31.289
Indeed,

05:31.372 --> 05:33.666
we know why Taniyama did those things.

05:35.168 --> 05:40.381
But we won it fair and square
so it's not our fault.

05:40.465 --> 05:43.801
No matter what is said,
we don't have to worry about Taniyama.

05:43.885 --> 05:45.094
Don't we?

05:45.178 --> 05:46.179
I know that.

05:46.763 --> 05:49.932
But we didn't actually win.

05:50.641 --> 05:52.268
Then what do you want to do?

05:52.351 --> 05:55.772
If we want to restore
Taniyama's reputation,

05:55.855 --> 05:59.358
then our victory
in the general meeting wouldn't count.

06:00.860 --> 06:02.278
I know that too.

06:02.945 --> 06:06.616
Anyway, that's about it
from a rational perspective.

06:07.366 --> 06:08.910
But it doesn't really matter.

06:08.993 --> 06:09.827
What?

06:09.911 --> 06:12.705
What's important is what you want to do.

06:13.414 --> 06:17.085
Of course, I want to help Taniyama.

06:17.168 --> 06:19.128
But that's...

06:19.212 --> 06:20.546
I know.

06:20.630 --> 06:22.131
Let's do it then.

06:22.215 --> 06:23.925
What? Is that okay?

06:24.008 --> 06:24.967
Yes.

06:25.051 --> 06:26.511
Rather than holding on to it now,

06:26.594 --> 06:30.181
it's better to settle things
and welcome the closing ceremony.

06:31.766 --> 06:32.767
I'm sorry.

06:32.850 --> 06:34.602
I said something troublesome.

06:34.685 --> 06:36.104
Don't worry about it.

06:36.187 --> 06:37.146
Didn't I tell you?

06:37.230 --> 06:38.189
I'll support you.

06:39.190 --> 06:40.900
Kuze.

06:45.905 --> 06:47.824
<i>There's someone over there.</i>

06:47.907 --> 06:49.617
Come closer.

06:49.700 --> 06:51.202
But...

06:51.285 --> 06:53.704
<i>It's totally like a rom-com.</i>

06:54.956 --> 06:56.082
<i>As a competent junior,</i>

06:56.165 --> 06:59.085
<i>I should act like nothing happened
and leave at a time like this.</i>

07:02.547 --> 07:04.173
<i>What's going on?</i>

07:04.257 --> 07:06.467
<i>Did I also trigger a rom-com event?</i>

07:08.302 --> 07:09.512
<i>This is no good.</i>

07:09.595 --> 07:11.472
<i>What's no good? Everything, of course.</i>

07:11.556 --> 07:12.807
<i>At this point,</i>

07:12.890 --> 07:15.601
<i>I have no choice but to forcefully change</i>

07:15.685 --> 07:19.313
<i>the course of the event!</i>

07:20.648 --> 07:23.484
So how long are you two going to hide?

07:23.568 --> 07:25.445
President, Sarashina.

07:26.446 --> 07:27.405
What?

07:29.532 --> 07:30.867
I'm sorry.

07:30.950 --> 07:33.286
We missed our timing to come out.

07:33.369 --> 07:34.871
That's right.

07:34.954 --> 07:38.166
We were just looking
for something that fell on the floor.

07:38.958 --> 07:39.876
Well then,

07:39.959 --> 07:42.128
let's just pretend that neither of us saw

07:42.211 --> 07:44.547
nor heard anything this time, okay?

07:44.630 --> 07:45.506
Okay.

07:45.590 --> 07:47.467
You're right. Let's do just that.

07:47.550 --> 07:49.177
It's a deal then.

07:49.260 --> 07:50.678
Let's go, Alya.

07:54.265 --> 07:56.392
Well, I...

07:56.476 --> 07:59.061
I still have other things to do.

08:06.152 --> 08:07.487
Hey, Nonoa.

08:07.570 --> 08:10.531
Don't you think Fymel's
new release is so cute?

08:11.657 --> 08:14.368
It doesn't really click with me.

08:14.452 --> 08:15.620
I see.

08:15.703 --> 08:18.289
If you don't like it, then forget it.

08:19.248 --> 08:21.209
<i>Such a powerful social presence.</i>

08:21.292 --> 08:22.835
<i>I can't even get close to her.</i>

08:23.419 --> 08:25.213
Forget about that, Nonoa.

08:25.296 --> 08:26.380
Can you come

08:26.464 --> 08:28.799
to my house party this Sunday?

08:28.883 --> 08:30.718
But the test is coming up.

08:30.801 --> 08:32.970
Well then, come over
and revise for the test.

08:33.054 --> 08:34.222
What?

08:34.305 --> 08:36.891
Don't you think
you've been a bit cold lately?

08:37.433 --> 08:40.394
No... I'm just kidding.

08:40.478 --> 08:41.354
A house party?

08:41.437 --> 08:42.980
Definitely count me in.

08:43.064 --> 08:44.190
Great!

08:44.273 --> 08:46.984
Hey, if Nonoa's going, I want to go too.

08:47.068 --> 08:49.028
Kuzecchi, do you need anything?

08:50.029 --> 08:51.948
Yeah, something like that.

08:52.031 --> 08:53.241
I see.

08:53.324 --> 08:55.076
You can't talk about it here?

08:55.159 --> 08:57.495
Yes, let's go somewhere else.

08:57.578 --> 08:58.996
Okay.

09:00.790 --> 09:01.791
So?

09:01.874 --> 09:03.584
If you want to confess, I'll accept it.

09:03.668 --> 09:05.378
But that's not why you're here, right?

09:05.461 --> 09:06.295
Yeah.

09:06.379 --> 09:08.381
Wait, you're willing
to accept my confession?

09:09.257 --> 09:10.800
Well, I'm single now.

09:10.883 --> 09:13.511
Besides, I don't hate you.

09:13.594 --> 09:16.389
No, don't date someone you don't hate.

09:16.472 --> 09:18.391
Date properly with someone you like.

09:18.474 --> 09:22.270
But I've never been
in a relationship with someone I like.

09:22.353 --> 09:24.647
Hey, that statement sounds a bit off.

09:24.730 --> 09:26.399
It can't be helped.

09:26.482 --> 09:29.402
I don't really know what love is.

09:30.570 --> 09:33.781
I don't mean
to criticize your views on love,

09:33.864 --> 09:37.785
but I think you shouldn't
degrade yourself.

09:40.329 --> 09:42.373
Sayacchi said that to me too.

09:42.456 --> 09:44.625
But she also slapped me when she said it.

09:44.709 --> 09:45.793
Seriously?

09:45.876 --> 09:48.462
She would slap her friend?

09:48.546 --> 09:50.923
Well, it was a special circumstance.

09:51.882 --> 09:54.135
Anyway, let's get back to the topic.

09:54.218 --> 09:55.303
What do you want?

09:56.304 --> 09:58.889
A lot of people are talking
about Taniyama, right?

09:58.973 --> 10:01.809
I'm wondering
if we can cool things down a bit.

10:03.269 --> 10:05.688
Does that bother you, Kuzecchi?

10:05.771 --> 10:08.399
It bothers my partner.

10:08.482 --> 10:10.067
I see.

10:10.776 --> 10:13.654
That's very kind of you.

10:14.864 --> 10:15.990
So?

10:16.073 --> 10:18.784
Why are you telling me this?

10:18.868 --> 10:21.579
I'm considered your enemy, aren't I?

10:22.079 --> 10:23.789
Enemy?

10:23.873 --> 10:25.750
I'm sure you noticed, Kuzecchi.

10:25.833 --> 10:28.294
I sent shills to instigate the audience.

10:28.377 --> 10:30.379
Of course, I did.

10:30.463 --> 10:32.465
You sent your friends as shills.

10:32.548 --> 10:35.593
How could you do something
that might cost you all your friends?

10:36.719 --> 10:37.678
To be honest,

10:37.762 --> 10:40.306
I'm not too attached to my friends
other than Sayacchi.

10:40.389 --> 10:43.809
Even if I lose them, it doesn't bother me.

10:44.769 --> 10:46.395
I'm curious about something.

10:47.855 --> 10:51.192
People like Taniyama
who hides her emotions deep inside

10:51.275 --> 10:54.278
are the type you find hardest
to understand, right?

10:54.362 --> 10:56.030
Why are you so attached to her?

10:57.031 --> 10:58.699
It's the opposite actually.

10:58.783 --> 11:01.077
I'm interested in her
and want to be with her

11:01.160 --> 11:02.745
because I don't understand her.

11:03.245 --> 11:04.789
Is that so?

11:04.872 --> 11:07.208
I'm sure you understand
this feeling too, Kuzecchi.

11:07.291 --> 11:11.045
When you see a brilliance that you lack,
you can't help but yearn for it.

11:11.962 --> 11:13.172
Then...

11:13.255 --> 11:16.801
as a fellow twisted person who yearns
for an honest and dazzling partner,

11:17.385 --> 11:19.387
let's come up with a wicked scheme.

11:19.470 --> 11:23.015
Well, it's not a wicked scheme per se.

11:23.641 --> 11:25.393
To put it simply,

11:25.476 --> 11:27.395
I'd like you to make up a plausible reason

11:27.478 --> 11:29.188
for Taniyama fleeing midway

11:29.271 --> 11:31.273
and spread it as a rumor.

11:31.357 --> 11:35.152
So you want people to think
that she didn't run away from the enemy?

11:35.653 --> 11:36.862
Is that okay?

11:36.946 --> 11:39.448
Your victory could become controversial.

11:39.532 --> 11:40.825
I know.

11:42.535 --> 11:43.744
All right.

11:43.828 --> 11:46.080
She was my partner anyway.

11:46.163 --> 11:49.125
It makes more sense for me
to take care of it.

11:49.667 --> 11:51.585
Then it's a deal.

11:51.669 --> 11:53.087
Thanks.

11:55.548 --> 11:57.967
<i>Is this one of those situations?</i>

11:58.050 --> 11:59.051
<i>If we were in a manga,</i>

11:59.135 --> 12:00.511
<i>she'd call her secret henchmen</i>

12:00.594 --> 12:02.596
<i>and give out orders like
"Chase after them"</i>

12:02.680 --> 12:04.098
<i>and "Don't get caught."</i>

12:05.057 --> 12:06.100
Ayano.

12:06.183 --> 12:07.393
Yes, Master Masachika?

12:07.476 --> 12:09.103
Why are you here?

12:10.146 --> 12:12.898
Because I think you called me.

12:13.774 --> 12:16.861
Hey, don't forget about me, Brother.

12:16.944 --> 12:19.613
No. Why are you guys here?

12:20.573 --> 12:21.490
No reason.

12:21.574 --> 12:26.120
I found out you were trying
to make contact with our enemy, Ms. Nonoa.

12:26.203 --> 12:27.621
So I got ahead of you

12:27.705 --> 12:29.707
and hid under the desk.

12:29.790 --> 12:31.375
Under the desk again?

12:31.959 --> 12:33.627
So what's the real reason?

12:33.711 --> 12:36.422
We wanted to roleplay
a secret meeting in an empty classroom.

12:36.505 --> 12:39.258
I didn't expect you
to start a real secret meeting.

12:39.341 --> 12:41.385
Seriously, what are you doing?

12:42.052 --> 12:43.762
Kuze, are you here?

12:49.852 --> 12:51.103
Alya?

12:51.187 --> 12:53.981
Did you misunderstand something?

12:54.064 --> 12:55.107
What misunderstanding?

12:55.191 --> 12:56.734
The three of you grew up together.

12:56.817 --> 12:59.778
It's not strange for you to play together.

12:59.862 --> 13:01.780
I'll get going now. Have fun.

13:01.864 --> 13:03.032
Alya.

13:03.616 --> 13:07.453
What? I can't believe you left me out.

13:08.370 --> 13:09.538
Bro.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.790
Judging by her face, I'm sure this is it.

13:11.874 --> 13:14.168
"I made lunch for Kuze
to thank him for helping me

13:14.251 --> 13:15.711
at the general meeting."

13:15.794 --> 13:17.171
"But where is he?"

13:17.254 --> 13:20.925
And then, she searched the whole
school premises to find this place.

13:21.008 --> 13:24.094
Don't make up your own stories!

13:35.731 --> 13:38.567
That was a different guy
from last time, right?

13:38.651 --> 13:40.277
Is that so?

13:40.361 --> 13:42.029
Anyway, he's my boyfriend now.

13:42.112 --> 13:44.031
A kiss won't make a difference, right?

13:50.496 --> 13:52.873
Don't degrade yourself.

13:52.957 --> 13:55.334
Take better care of yourself!

13:58.295 --> 14:00.464
You didn't have to get so mad.

14:01.674 --> 14:03.884
Nonoa, you're finally back.

14:03.968 --> 14:05.803
What did you two talk about?

14:05.886 --> 14:08.889
We were just talking about Sayacchi.

14:08.973 --> 14:10.391
She took the day off.

14:10.474 --> 14:12.851
Kuzecchi wanted to ask what happened.

14:12.935 --> 14:14.603
Taniyama took the day off?

14:14.687 --> 14:16.605
Is it because she lost the debate?

14:16.689 --> 14:18.482
No, no.

14:18.566 --> 14:20.150
It's actually because of me.

14:20.234 --> 14:21.068
Speaking of which,

14:21.151 --> 14:23.112
Sayacchi gave up on the debate

14:23.195 --> 14:24.822
because of me too.

14:24.905 --> 14:25.906
What?

14:25.990 --> 14:27.032
What do you mean?

14:27.116 --> 14:29.702
Actually, at the general meeting that day,

14:29.785 --> 14:32.413
I planted some shills in the audience.

14:32.496 --> 14:33.914
Sayacchi found out about it.

14:34.456 --> 14:35.583
Something like that.

14:36.876 --> 14:41.255
I just happened
to run into Yuki and Ayano.

14:42.840 --> 14:44.800
You don't look convinced at all.

14:44.884 --> 14:45.926
That's not true.

14:46.010 --> 14:48.095
Actually, you don't have
to hide it from me.

14:48.178 --> 14:51.015
Isn't it good to be close
to childhood friends?

14:52.766 --> 14:54.518
By the way,

14:54.602 --> 14:57.271
do you want to study together
after school today?

14:58.689 --> 15:00.232
Are you kidding me?

15:00.316 --> 15:02.109
Hey, that's too rude.

15:08.616 --> 15:10.576
Excuse me, Alya?

15:10.659 --> 15:11.785
What is it?

15:11.869 --> 15:14.371
Don't you think you're a little too close?

15:14.455 --> 15:16.415
Is that a problem?

15:16.498 --> 15:18.000
No, it's not.

15:18.500 --> 15:19.543
<i>It's fine.</i>

15:19.627 --> 15:22.212
<i>As long as no one sees us...</i>

15:22.296 --> 15:23.130
Oh, my.

15:23.213 --> 15:24.673
I'm so sorry.

15:24.757 --> 15:26.050
I didn't knock.

15:26.133 --> 15:28.552
<i>Little Sister!</i>

15:28.636 --> 15:30.429
Are you studying for the exam?

15:31.597 --> 15:35.059
If you don't mind, can we join you?

15:35.684 --> 15:36.644
Yes, I do mind.

15:37.394 --> 15:38.520
Alya.

15:38.604 --> 15:39.688
What do you think

15:39.772 --> 15:40.814
about what Yuki said?

15:40.898 --> 15:42.274
Sure.

15:42.358 --> 15:43.984
No reason to turn them down.

15:44.068 --> 15:44.944
I see.

15:45.527 --> 15:46.695
Thank you.

15:47.279 --> 15:49.406
I wanted it to be just the two of us.

15:49.490 --> 15:50.532
<i>Seriously, this girl.</i>

15:50.616 --> 15:52.326
<i>Don't say something so adorable!</i>

15:57.998 --> 16:02.044
You've only been looking
at the answer sheet.

16:02.127 --> 16:04.588
Are you really studying for the exam?

16:04.672 --> 16:08.592
It's a waste of time to ponder
on a question you don't understand.

16:08.676 --> 16:10.052
If you have time for that,

16:10.135 --> 16:12.596
it's faster to memorize all the solutions.

16:12.680 --> 16:15.391
Then you can't apply it properly.

16:16.266 --> 16:17.184
It's fine.

16:17.893 --> 16:20.521
Masachika has always been like this.

16:20.604 --> 16:21.855
Right, Ayano?

16:21.939 --> 16:22.898
Yes.

16:22.982 --> 16:26.110
Master Masachika
has always studied like this.

16:29.822 --> 16:32.241
Ayano, is there anything
you don't understand?

16:33.200 --> 16:34.118
No.

16:34.743 --> 16:36.704
Actually, there is.

16:37.204 --> 16:38.288
Where?

16:38.372 --> 16:39.206
It's okay.

16:39.289 --> 16:42.501
There's no need to trouble you
with such a trivial matter.

16:42.584 --> 16:43.711
Don't be shy.

16:43.794 --> 16:45.379
I won't look down on you.

16:45.963 --> 16:46.797
No.

16:46.880 --> 16:48.424
At a time like this, I'd rather you

16:48.507 --> 16:50.884
mercilessly call me "a useless person."

16:51.385 --> 16:52.886
I won't say that.

16:52.970 --> 16:55.222
I... see.

16:55.305 --> 16:56.807
Why do you look disappointed?

16:57.516 --> 16:59.309
Hey, are you guys really

16:59.393 --> 17:01.270
just childhood friends?

17:02.396 --> 17:03.230
Yes.

17:03.313 --> 17:04.148
Why do you ask?

17:04.231 --> 17:05.399
Why...

17:05.482 --> 17:08.110
It's just that
you say you're childhood friends,

17:08.193 --> 17:10.070
but the way you interact seems distant.

17:11.613 --> 17:13.782
Everyone, thanks for the hard work.

17:18.454 --> 17:21.915
Masha's black tea is the best.

17:21.999 --> 17:23.208
Oh, my. What's this?

17:24.668 --> 17:28.005
I think it's a book
that Sarashina confiscated.

17:28.088 --> 17:30.007
A FOOLPROOF GUIDE
TO STARTING HYPNOSIS

17:30.591 --> 17:32.593
Alya, try to hypnotize me.

17:32.676 --> 17:33.510
I don't want to.

17:33.594 --> 17:35.721
What? Why?

17:35.804 --> 17:38.390
I want to experience hypnosis too.

17:38.474 --> 17:40.476
I want to try it too.

17:40.559 --> 17:42.603
I told you, I won't.

17:43.479 --> 17:45.189
Then you try it, Kuze.

17:45.272 --> 17:46.690
What? Me?

17:46.774 --> 17:49.902
It's because Alya is so cold.

17:49.985 --> 17:52.321
Well, I guess that's fine.

17:53.489 --> 17:55.908
The first step is... hypnosis induction?

17:55.991 --> 17:57.117
I can't wait!

17:57.201 --> 17:58.368
Let's see.

17:58.452 --> 18:01.371
Okay, "please look at this finger."

18:01.455 --> 18:02.289
Finger?

18:02.372 --> 18:03.415
That's what it says.

18:03.499 --> 18:04.666
I see.

18:08.545 --> 18:12.007
"Your consciousness will start to fade."

18:12.508 --> 18:14.968
"And please keep looking at this finger."

18:15.469 --> 18:16.428
"Okay."

18:16.512 --> 18:19.306
"You're losing consciousness."

18:20.390 --> 18:22.601
"After I clap my hands,

18:22.684 --> 18:25.521
you'll fall into the world of dreams."

18:26.063 --> 18:28.982
"Three, two, one, asleep."

18:30.275 --> 18:31.944
What? Masha?

18:32.027 --> 18:33.487
Masha?

18:33.570 --> 18:36.448
Did it really work?

18:36.532 --> 18:39.284
All right, cut it out.

18:40.160 --> 18:41.578
Masha?

18:41.662 --> 18:42.913
Anyway,

18:42.996 --> 18:45.207
let me undo the hypnosis first.

18:45.707 --> 18:46.708
Let's see.

18:46.792 --> 18:49.086
"When I touch your shoulder,

18:49.169 --> 18:51.088
the hypnosis will be broken."

18:51.171 --> 18:52.714
"One, two, wake up."

18:57.427 --> 19:00.097
Well, Kuze, what's next?

19:00.681 --> 19:01.515
What?

19:01.598 --> 19:02.432
Come on.

19:02.516 --> 19:05.310
Doesn't it say to clap
after you raise your finger?

19:05.394 --> 19:06.228
No...

19:06.311 --> 19:08.355
What? Don't you remember?

19:08.438 --> 19:10.023
What? Remember what?

19:10.107 --> 19:10.941
Masha.

19:11.024 --> 19:12.818
Seriously, stop pretending.

19:13.318 --> 19:14.319
Well then, Alya.

19:14.403 --> 19:17.990
Why don't you try getting
hypnotized by Masachika too?

19:18.574 --> 19:19.491
- What?
- What?

19:19.575 --> 19:21.201
If you feel the effect,

19:21.285 --> 19:22.911
it'll remove your doubts, right?

19:25.372 --> 19:27.124
All right. I'm ready.

19:27.207 --> 19:28.417
Are we really doing this?

19:28.500 --> 19:29.501
Don't ask.

19:29.585 --> 19:32.212
I'll put an end to this farce in no time.

19:32.296 --> 19:35.424
Then, "please look at this finger."

19:36.717 --> 19:38.510
She's so gullible.

19:39.469 --> 19:41.096
By the way,

19:41.180 --> 19:44.391
why was Masha hypnotized too?

19:44.474 --> 19:45.392
Who knows?

19:45.475 --> 19:46.351
Seriously?

19:46.435 --> 19:47.811
We can do so much erotic stuff.

19:47.895 --> 19:49.271
Even so, don't say it out loud!

19:50.397 --> 19:52.608
It's time for an otaku quiz.

19:52.691 --> 19:53.609
Here's the question.

19:53.692 --> 19:55.444
A beautiful woman
is accidentally hypnotized.

19:55.944 --> 19:57.196
When it comes to the first cue,

19:57.279 --> 19:58.280
what is it usually?

19:58.363 --> 19:59.698
Let her regress to a baby!

19:59.781 --> 20:02.409
Make her more open
and take off her clothes!

20:02.492 --> 20:03.619
Well...

20:03.702 --> 20:08.540
Maybe make her tell me
some embarrassing secrets?

20:08.624 --> 20:10.375
You said to make her more open.

20:10.459 --> 20:11.793
Isn't that too general?

20:11.877 --> 20:14.087
Regressing to a baby
is too aggressive, right?

20:15.255 --> 20:16.465
Ayano's suggestion.

20:16.548 --> 20:18.008
It's not bad,

20:18.091 --> 20:19.176
but it's a bit too weak.

20:19.801 --> 20:20.636
In that sense,

20:20.719 --> 20:24.306
my suggestion to make her more open
was absolutely the correct answer.

20:24.389 --> 20:27.476
Besides, she might also reveal
some embarrassing secrets.

20:27.559 --> 20:30.103
You even considered my answer.

20:30.187 --> 20:31.438
Amazing, Mistress Yuki.

20:31.521 --> 20:34.066
All right. I win by majority vote.

20:36.902 --> 20:37.819
Alya.

20:37.903 --> 20:38.820
Masha.

20:38.904 --> 20:41.990
Your personalities will gradually open up

20:42.491 --> 20:43.659
and you'll lose your wits.

20:43.742 --> 20:46.662
Strip your bodies and minds naked.

20:51.166 --> 20:52.209
What? What?

20:52.292 --> 20:54.086
Did it really work?

20:56.713 --> 20:57.589
What?

21:02.052 --> 21:03.303
Hey, Yuki.

21:03.387 --> 21:06.181
Why am I being patted endlessly here?

21:07.391 --> 21:09.601
There, there.

21:09.685 --> 21:12.688
Who knows? I wonder why?

21:12.771 --> 21:14.356
Hey, look over here, you criminal!

21:14.439 --> 21:16.400
I can't believe it wasn't Masachika,

21:16.483 --> 21:19.194
but Masha who established a harem.

21:19.278 --> 21:21.405
You're shocked about the weirdest thing.

21:21.947 --> 21:23.907
There, there.

21:23.991 --> 21:25.701
Well, Masha.

21:25.784 --> 21:27.786
Can you let go of me now?

21:28.996 --> 21:29.997
No.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.373
You can't?

21:31.957 --> 21:33.875
So annoying.

21:35.460 --> 21:37.004
It's in the way.

21:37.087 --> 21:39.256
Alya? What do you want?

21:48.223 --> 21:49.808
That's the morning look of a skilled

21:49.891 --> 21:51.435
but lazy-at-home office lady!

21:51.518 --> 21:52.352
I get you!

21:56.106 --> 21:57.190
No! Wait!

21:57.274 --> 21:59.860
Why are they all stripping?

21:59.943 --> 22:01.528
Come to think of it,

22:01.611 --> 22:03.530
I think I ordered them
to gradually open up

22:03.613 --> 22:05.866
and strip their bodies and minds naked.

22:07.951 --> 22:09.202
Let's see.

22:09.286 --> 22:11.121
Well then, when I touch your shoulder,

22:11.204 --> 22:12.456
the hypnosis will be broken.

22:12.539 --> 22:14.374
One, two, wake up.

22:15.208 --> 22:16.626
Hey, isn't it still in effect?

22:17.336 --> 22:18.337
What?

22:18.420 --> 22:20.297
Well then, when I touch your shoulder,

22:20.380 --> 22:21.882
the hypnosis will be broken.

22:22.507 --> 22:24.384
One, two, wake up.

22:26.094 --> 22:28.013
Oh, no. I can't undo it either.

22:28.096 --> 22:29.806
Seriously?

22:29.890 --> 22:31.516
Wait, what should we do?

22:32.100 --> 22:32.934
Masha.

22:33.018 --> 22:35.604
I'm done with my stuff.

22:36.688 --> 22:39.191
What's going on?

22:39.274 --> 22:40.901
Sarashina.

22:40.984 --> 22:42.819
Well, it's like this.

22:42.903 --> 22:46.198
I tried the hypnosis in the book just now,

22:46.281 --> 22:48.408
but I couldn't undo it.

22:51.119 --> 22:52.537
Excuse my rudeness.

22:57.709 --> 22:58.585
Hold on.

22:58.668 --> 23:00.545
What did you just do?

23:00.629 --> 23:02.297
What? I just did a reset.

23:02.380 --> 23:03.548
What?

23:07.135 --> 23:08.428
That's strange.

23:08.512 --> 23:10.806
Why am I lying on the sofa?

23:10.889 --> 23:11.932
Oh my?

23:12.015 --> 23:12.933
Well,

23:13.016 --> 23:15.435
I know you must be confused now.

23:15.519 --> 23:17.896
But you should tidy yourself up first.

23:18.396 --> 23:19.689
What?

23:20.357 --> 23:22.275
Tidy up?

23:27.239 --> 23:28.907
What is going on?

23:28.990 --> 23:30.408
Oh, no!

23:30.492 --> 23:32.119
By the way, Kuze,

23:32.202 --> 23:33.370
you saw everything, right?

23:36.248 --> 23:38.166
Do you need a reset from me?
